<header><p class="st-kicker">republic · Mesopotamia and Iran</p><h1 class="st-title">Republic of Iraq</h1><p class="st-meta">1958 CE – present · capital Baghdad</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The Iraqi state since the 1958 revolution: military regimes, Ba'athist dictatorship under Saddam Hussein, war and occupation, and a federal democracy since 2005.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>On 14 July 1958 the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/free-officers-movement-iraq">Free Officers</a> under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abd-al-karim-qasim">Abd al-Karim Qasim</a> overthrew the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-iraq">Kingdom of Iraq</a> and proclaimed a republic. Qasim left the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baghdad-pact">Baghdad Pact</a>, began land reform and claimed <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/state-of-kuwait">Kuwait</a>, but was killed in a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baath-party">Ba'athist</a> coup in 1963. The Arif brothers then ruled until the Ba'ath Party took power again in 1968.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ahmed-hassan-al-bakr">Ahmad Hasan al-Bakr</a> and, from 1979, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saddam-hussein">Saddam Hussein</a>, oil wealth funded development alongside a pervasive police state. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iraq">Iraq</a> fought <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iran">Iran</a> from 1980 to 1988, conducted the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anfal-campaign">Anfal campaign</a> against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kurds">Kurds</a>, including the gas attack on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/halabja-massacre">Halabja</a>, and invaded <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/state-of-kuwait">Kuwait</a> in 1990, leading to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gulf-war">Gulf War</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sanctions">sanctions</a>. A US-led invasion in 2003 overthrew Saddam, and a 2005 constitution created a federal parliamentary system with a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kurdistan">Kurdistan</a> Region.</p><h2>To the present</h2><p>Sectarian war followed in 2006 to 2008, and the Islamic State seized <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mosul">Mosul</a> in 2014 before its defeat in 2017. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iraq">Iraq</a> remains a federal parliamentary republic, governed through power-sharing between Shia, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sunni-islam">Sunni</a> and Kurdish parties.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/republic-of-iraq.jpg" alt="Republic of Iraq" width="320" height="213"><figcaption>Image: See File history below for details. · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Iraq.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1958 CE – present</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/21st-century">21st century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>republic</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>bureaucratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Baghdad</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Abd al-Karim Qasim, Saddam Hussein, Nouri al-Maliki</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Shia and Sunni Islam</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Arabic, Kurdish</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/iraq">Iraq</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Iraqi Republic, Iraq</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1992&amp;focus=republic-of-iraq" aria-label="Republic of Iraq on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5814 968 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Republic of Iraq lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M6134 1224L6134 1224"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M6134 1224h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M6134 1224h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M6134 1224h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Baghdad. <a href="/atlas?year=1992&amp;focus=republic-of-iraq">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
